outines, and navigating common real life scenarios through role plays and guided practice. Reading proficiency develops through work with the Bangla script, shop signs, short informational texts, and authentic materials, while writing proficiency grows through script practice, completing personal information forms, composing simple sentences, and writing short notes and descriptions. The course also supports a heritage learner pathway: students who speak or understand Bangla at home but have little or no literacy in the script often begin in BENGL 1121, where they can strengthen their oral skills while building systematic reading, writing, and grammar foundations. Designed for true beginners and heritage learners without prior literacy experience.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": "", "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": null, "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": "", "catalogCoreq": "", "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "catalogName": null, "catalogNextOffered": null, "lastTermsOffered": "2026FA, 2025FA, 2024FA, 2023FA", "catalogCredits": null, "catalogGradeOption": null, "catalogLocation": null, "catalogCrosslisted": null, "catalogCrosslistings": null, "catalogComeets": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2937, "crseId": 354532, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "BENGL", "catalogNbr": "2201", "titleShort": "Interm Bangla-Bengali I", "titleLong": "Intermediate Bangla-Bengali I", "crseAttrs": [{"crseAttr": "0004", "crseAttrValue": "SALANG", "descr": "South Asia Studies Lang", "descrformal": "South Asia Studies Language", "attrDescr": "Exploratory Studies", "attrDescrShort": "ExplStudy"}, {"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "FL-AG", "descr": "AG-Foreign Language", "descrformal": "AG-Foreign